  "mechanismSummary": "After the MPV reduction, the aluminium alkoxide next to the ester closes a γ-lactone (a five-membered lactone). The ester C=O binds the aluminium that holds the alkoxide, the alkoxide moves onto the activated ester carbon to give a tetrahedral intermediate, methoxide is taken up by aluminium as the C=O re-forms, and the lactone is released. This only works because the alkoxide and the ester are cis on the folded ring system. Woodward isolated this hydroxy lactone from the MPV reaction; the stepwise picture on aluminium is a reasonable mechanism, not one he proved. The other alkoxide is drawn as the free alcohol (released by exchange with isopropanol, as in the warm-up), and the aluminium is drawn as a single molecule.",
